// json_ctor — SELF-HOSTED json.stringify: a thin delegation to the PROVEN
// value_core implementation (the native runtime does exactly the same:
// `almide_rt_json_stringify` forwards to `almide_rt_value_stringify`).
// Registered as a separate impl fn because the auto-link renames one impl to
// one call name. The `json_object` / `json_array` twins that lived here were
// the retired `json.object` / `json.array` aliases, dropped with the E040
// window — construction is `value.object` / `value.array`.
fn json_stringify(v: Value) -> String = value.stringify(v)
